==========================================================================
(1) Gauss-sum iota-parity  (p = 3 mod 4 => g = i*sqrt(p), IMAGINARY = iota-ODD)
==========================================================================
  g(3) = 0.00000+1.73205j   |g|^2=3.000 (=p=3);  i*sqrt(3) = 0.00000+1.73205j  => i*sqrt(p) (iota-ODD, p=3mod4)
  g(7) = 0.00000+2.64575j   |g|^2=7.000 (=p=7);  i*sqrt(7) = 0.00000+2.64575j  => i*sqrt(p) (iota-ODD, p=3mod4)
  g(11) = 0.00000+3.31662j   |g|^2=11.000 (=p=11);  i*sqrt(11) = 0.00000+3.31662j  => i*sqrt(p) (iota-ODD, p=3mod4)
  g(19) = 0.00000+4.35890j   |g|^2=19.000 (=p=19);  i*sqrt(19) = 0.00000+4.35890j  => i*sqrt(p) (iota-ODD, p=3mod4)

==========================================================================
(2) THE CROSS-TERM  g(3)*g(7) = i*sqrt3 * i*sqrt7 = -sqrt21  (iota-ODD (x) iota-ODD -> iota-EVEN)
==========================================================================
  g(3)*g(7) = -4.58258+0.00000j   (imag ~ 0 => REAL);  -sqrt21 = -4.58258
  sqrt21 = 4.58258 = sqrt(3*7);  in Q(sqrt-3,sqrt-7): sqrt21 = (i*sqrt3)(i*sqrt7)/(-1)
  g(21) composite (char mod 21 = (.|3)(.|7)): 4.58258+0.00000j  (real, ~ +-sqrt21*unit)
  Gal(Q(sqrt-3,sqrt-7)) = Z2 x Z2; fixed fields Q(sqrt-3),Q(sqrt-7),Q(sqrt21); sqrt21 needs BOTH primes

==========================================================================
(3) THE 21 = 3*7 BRIDGE  (flip-rank obstruction  <->  LRC sqrt21 certificate)
==========================================================================
  |Aut(Paley_7)| = 21 = 3*7  = argmax|Aut| = the n=7 flip-rank OBSTRUCTION (HYP-3817, opus-S15)
  norm(sqrt21)   = 21 = 3*7  = the OPEN-Q-108 residual cross-term (opus-S26 HYP-3818)
  Paley_7 CAYLEY spectrum: cos(theta) = -(7-1)/(7+1) = -3/4  <=>  eig(S)=+-i*sqrt7 = g(7) (HYP-3814)
  SHARED prime 3 = Eisenstein/covering (Phi6(14)=183=3*61);  7 = heptagon/odd index (14=2*7)
  => the covering obstruction (|Aut|=21) and the certificate residual (sqrt21) are the SAME 3*7 arithmetic:
     3 (iota-odd i*sqrt3, covering) x 7 (iota-odd i*sqrt7, odd index) -> 21 (iota-even sqrt21, residual).
  The flip-rank obstruction is a COVERING witness (fixed-point/atom, HYP-3817);
  the sqrt21 residual is its MOMENT/certificate shadow -- 'reach for a covering or a moment, not a transform.'
